---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const scale = [
  { range: '9.5 to 10', word: 'Exceptional', meaning: 'One of the best I have had. I would replace it the day it ran out.' },
  { range: '8.5 to 9.4', word: 'Excellent', meaning: 'Does almost everything right. Easy to recommend.' },
  { range: '7.5 to 8.4', word: 'Very good', meaning: 'Glad to have it. One or two things hold it back.' },
  { range: '6.5 to 7.4', word: 'Good', meaning: 'Enjoyable, with clear reservations. Right for some people, not for everyone.' },
  { range: '5 to 6.4', word: 'Fine', meaning: 'Nothing wrong, nothing memorable. Not worth seeking out.' },
  { range: 'Below 5', word: 'Not recommended', meaning: 'Flawed in a way that is hard to get past.' },
];
---

<Base title="How I score" description="What the scores on CaskScents mean, and how each bottle earns them.">
  <article class="wrap page">
    <p class="label">About</p>
    <h1 class="display">How I score</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Every bottle gets a score out of 10, to one decimal place. The numbers mean the same thing for a
      whiskey as for a fragrance.
    </p>

    <dl class="scale">
      {
        scale.map((step) => (
          <div>
            <dt>
              <span class="score">{step.range}</span>
              <span class="display word">{step.word}</span>
            </dt>
            <dd>{step.meaning}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>

    <h2 class="display">What goes into it</h2>
    <ul class="points">
      <li>
        <strong>Whiskey</strong> is scored on nose, palate and finish.
        <strong>Fragrance</strong> is scored on scent, longevity, sillage and the bottle itself.
      </li>
      <li>Each of those scores comes with a line saying why it earned it.</li>
      <li>
        The overall score is my judgment of the whole bottle. It is not an average, so it can sit a little
        above or below the others.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Price never changes a score.</strong> A review says in words whether the bottle is worth the money,
        and shows the price, so you can weigh that for yourself.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Bottles and samples.</strong> Some reviews come from my own bottle and some from a sample. Each
        review says which. A fragrance tried from a sample gets no score for the bottle itself.
      </li>
      <li>Scores are one person's palate and nose. Use them as a starting point, not a verdict.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    max-width: 52rem;
    padding-block: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3.5rem) var(--section-pad);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-4xl);
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--bone-soft);
  }
  .scale {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .scale div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.25rem 2rem;
    padding-block: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  dt {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .score {
    min-width: 6.5rem;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
  .word {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
  }
  dd {
    color: var(--bone-soft);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .points {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--bone-soft);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .points li {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    position: relative;
  }
  .points li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.75em;
    width: 0.5rem;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--gold);
  }
  strong {
    color: var(--bone);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .scale div {
      grid-template-columns: 20rem 1fr;
      align-items: baseline;
    }
  }
</style>
